, protect me, O Rāghava?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.849,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065021","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"950e60bd08fc58df0791ece6a79100aad2825ea31d9710798f9499a8453ab22b","compact":"1fde656574eadcda1c2f7f05b59aa6a6c64d502fcb7667449f18755ad44a4073","nasal":"1fde656574eadcda1c2f7f05b59aa6a6c64d502fcb7667449f18755ad44a4073"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-22","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":22,"english":"Those two best of men, gifted with the effulgence of Wind and Fire, and incapable of being repressed even by the celestials, are disregarding me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065022","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7d4ed2196f329822881a88c49259a6eadc8b576744e5edc1016f8a9f1a25a571","compact":"607d49bca40533e0b3abe63eace67fd2c753282af89811a9df6defe9751bc8a6","nasal":"607d49bca40533e0b3abe63eace67fd2c753282af89811a9df6defe9751bc8a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-23","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":23,"english":"Forsooth have I perpetrated a mighty iniquity since those two slayers of foes, being capable, do not protect me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065023","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16d42d4ab3f088169288455b1be7c37bfd2685429849eb80c50ea38da5af1ddc","compact":"59cc3933ad8db89bb09b1e7712303ba31e5d147584bbb9ae230757b34c450007","nasal":"59cc3933ad8db89bb09b1e7712303ba31e5d147584bbb9ae230757b34c450007"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-24","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":24,"english":"Hearing those sweet and piteous accents of Vaidehi I again spoke to that worshipful dame, saying. 'Forsooth can I swear by you, O worshipful dame, that Rāma is sorely stricken with grief in your absence. And Lakšmaņa too relent heavily beholding him laden with sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.603,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065024","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2fe8d8ae0503117cd01e9291ca9395d688a07eb6a2bcb1f11ddbf059f3f026d","compact":"2893b4461f5165713dfd0ec0be107435f17a46a2336eaec1203e0e1f23d9bafe","nasal":"4fa534ebe168a840c8e11a499375cc3c8e48a943c6682f12db2f6f74968e1541"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-25","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":25,"english":"Hearing those sweet and piteous accents of Vaidehi I again spoke to that worshipful dame, saying. 'Forsooth can I swear by you, O worshipful dame, that Rāma is sorely stricken with grief in your absence. And Lakšmaņa too relent heavily beholding him laden with sorrow.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065025","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2ade3cb43b02c31bb85c59fe8f9a68c14bcfc289cec461242672b82903ab625","compact":"5b9a6d39ca3be229fdaeb7872dd6c477dd305e67c9fff9f840dd81ae38e8638b","nasal":"5b9a6d39ca3be229fdaeb7872dd6c477dd305e67c9fff9f840dd81ae38e8638b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-26","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":26,"english":"It dose not behove you to relent any more as I have succeeded in finding you out. You shall at this very moment behold the end of your grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"950a0f050c7d5fa0546183c23f73d44f6d4c8de3500e0665ba1ef5b67fbad2eb","compact":"ee6aca0321c9bdfb779493b1cebc64b2699a53039f572ef812114dd108dfb64c","nasal":"ca7391507989ff41e7676715b39e52a9c9099703746e4fa41d8a669bbc890026"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":27,"english":"And those two princes, the foremost of men and slayers of foes, actuated with energy on hearing that I have seen you, shall reduce Lankā to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65e1895b6a34540584be7de819dca832a9ed46a65246218b7c7078ffe9cdf53c","compact":"3da10eb2412a99b42aa2cca097bcfa7d077fdc1b1b31c732b5c82dd7488db0b2","nasal":"a5c21bb4c9b8cbd12a95793d8969af1d046861a56561e9ff71504cb0b3df5a09"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":28,"english":"And slaying in conflict the terrible Rāvaņa, with his kith and kin, Rāghava, in sooth, O excellent damsel, shall take you back to his own city.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.547,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09f54fd220e4873328e0156483829cd6dfe96bf68e8c312b440eab720ed19106","compact":"a95c87852728ab2857c12fefeaea2857dcb18a5fb4df0da3c82131d05731fff9","nasal":"c6c5b2ee8bc3ac91f7a765e42310c870132b9647de8159f0abce0f1f36d319bd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":29,"english":"O you of a blameless person, do you confer on me such a token, as might be recognized by Ráma and conduce to his pleasure.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"43f1b886ec36edbc6b13bfd73bed18aacace3462616921c0f931fc08e349012e","compact":"ced99397c37ec175a3c7fd078d4451e46f3d3d147a4851a34b2147849a44669e","nasal":"8493f48477d7c3b9ea925211dcf54492ac98056963da40d37858e9d2df810fb0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":30,"english":"Thereat, casting her looks around, she took out an excellent jewel from her cloth, worthy of being set on her braid and conferred it on me, O you of great strength.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59211032c9050b330fea827ac615611f29eea53d42ebb18819fcc81f47e252dd","compact":"fe7f0e8e5f80226ff385f7c3126e1622ef13d24508e5f9143c159c977fae327d","nasal":"65827016339193f514394801fd88789424815bb602962b37c82ee829839c92f5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":31,"english":"O you, the most favourite of the Raghu race, taking for you that gem with my hands and bowing to her, I addressed myself speedily for departure.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.464,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"850fbfb1574a9e652eb742b67836b6f60a514d1fc7ec7c0b5abd5b6af32c34e9","compact":"0e83632d200e4941ac4e21239346cdad9c3e2bde27a23ff02dad79b25ccf1a68","nasal":"0e83632d200e4941ac4e21239346cdad9c3e2bde27a23ff02dad79b25ccf1a68"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-32","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":32,"english":"Thereupon beholding me ready to depart and increase in bulk and about to leap up in the welkin, Sītā, the daughter of the king Janaka, poorly, bathed in tears, overwhelmed with sorrow and having her voice choked with grief, saying 'Blessed are you O great monkey, since you shall behold the large-armed and the lotuseyed Ráma and the highly famed Lakşmaņa, my lord's younger brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.854,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065032","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5a4d338f24c22f51996832c2421b221d7b44201547db37e4c61a008134e9b99f","compact":"cd5ccf59b57b631cad9dc30ff5b4b65f157308570aed1be20566c5d53d64bd15","nasal":"cd5ccf59b57b631cad9dc30ff5b4b65f157308570aed1be20566c5d53d64bd15"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-33","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":33,"english":"Addressing me with these words she again said-O Hanuman, do you relate my well-being to Rāma and Lakshamana of leonine prowess, and Sugrīva accompanied by his followers.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.953,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065033","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9c5fbd7d9f1ca11b58b37796ec6bdf4c3f0d286720a8443e802a35cebbaf39a9","compact":"99ac6d58cc820d90e4dcb3c734fb5b3f67aa9feca9eab2a6368f57951c7eb3a1","nasal":"99ac6d58cc820d90e4dcb3c734fb5b3f67aa9feca9eab2a6368f57951c7eb3a1"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-34","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":34,"english":"Do you so describe as the large-armed Rāghava may save me from this ocean of grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.541,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065034","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0d35964de06289e75bef39cf4f8935afc294a6de4f5b2eef97f2dd7f1265e52b","compact":"27dfc1a48f11dcff22ddf5c5f96df2cc46af05a18900544e43b685e45c944d1b","nasal":"63af5b74469d721288caacb4f90f1c4f3678cce7934f051d1eb23d6de3574331"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-35","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":35,"english":"Do you narrate to Rāma this my terrible sorrow and the affliction by the she-demons. May good betide you, on your way, O foremost of the monkeys.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065035","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fb18d1f6faad09a899a23daddb8f85de7c8ddc74b440062f84171e2991f10fcc","compact":"3e819dddf2c67bdcd05fc93c8638f883f85f3259885d2de6aef5c5512a5ca361","nasal":"3e819dddf2c67bdcd05fc93c8638f883f85f3259885d2de6aef5c5512a5ca361"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-65-36","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":65,"verse":36,"english":"Thus the worshipful Sítă gave vent to these piteous accents. Hearing these words do you believe that it is all well with her.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.753,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-67-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5065036","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9295a27f8064c4e5b41625d8dc028a5450497d747781e455092fff9e071fa3c3","compact":"acae165d1f0375e54a361342d08c6e1701c6260bad77385ba1718f1ffcf6d8db","nasal":"acae165d1f0375e54a361342d08c6e1701c6260bad77385ba1718f1ffcf6d8db"}}]
